  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;be two unit vectors such that the angle between them is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is the angle between the vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>164</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
